(i) any insurable property is exposed to maritime perils;
C.Sivadasan vs The New India Assurance Co on 25 March, 2011 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/152045970/
14 (ii) the earnings or acquisition of any freight, passage money, commission, profit or other pecuniary benefit,or the security for any advances, loans, or disbursements is endangered by the exposure of insurable property to maritime perils;
(iii) any liability to a third party may be incurred by the owner of or other person interested in or responsible for, insurable property by reason of maritime perils."
